Explicit admissible family for rule C: s(x,y,z) = f(y,z) xor g(x,z) xor h(x,y).
  random f,g,h on L=5: violated cubes = 0

Cubic covariance of rule C: the set of 8 corners of a unit cube is mapped to the corners of a unit cube
by every element of O_h and every translation (checked over all 48 signed permutations):
  all 48 map the unit cube to a unit cube: True

Contrast: binary NN hard-core rule (no two adjacent 1s) on L^3 open boxes (brute force, small L)
  L=2: sites=8, N_adm=35, log2=5.129, per site=0.641
  lower bound for any L: every subset of one sublattice is admissible -> log2 N_adm >= floor(L^3/2) (volume law)
